From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 75/75] PC5: a game's memory counts kept for a second, as counting
 them held Wine's memory lock all the time for an Unreal Engine 5 game that
 asks every few milliseconds (Wine patch 0989)

Gears of War: E-Day ran on about one core at 0 to 1 frames a second: several of its threads asked for the process's memory counts about every 10 ms, and each count walked every view's pages with the lock every allocation and page fault waits for. Wine patch 0989 keeps the counts for a second.
